":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary model paper on genomic language models, but the evidence only describes DNA/genomic sequence modeling. No natural-language text component or text-bio bridge is supported.","evidence_snippet":"\"genomic language modeling (gLM)\"; \"trained five byte-pair encoding tokenizers and pretrained 52 gLMs\"; \"DNA sequences can be conceptualized as a complex language\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_002410","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The paper presents new genomic language models with large-scale pretraining on 19,551 genomes and compares transferable performance across many tasks. The abstract does not explicitly state a decoder/autoregressive/generative mechanism, so generative status is unclear.","evidence_snippet":"\"trained five byte-pair encoding tokenizers and pretrained 52 gLMs\"; \"19,551 reference genomes\"; \"outperforms... in 13 of 19 benchmarking phenotypic predictions\"; \"continual pretraining, domain adaptation\"; \"future genomic language models\"}]}]}"},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"EC2_no_text_component","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes"}}}]

